---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Why the most expensive person in your organisation isn't the CEO" description="The business case for human-centric management — with the evidence to prove it.">
  
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="greenhouse-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <span class="hero-label">The Greenhouse</span>
      <h1>Why the most expensive person in your organisation isn't the CEO</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Harvard data proves your high-performers might be bankrupting you. 
        This is the business case for being human — and the 90-day pilot to prove it works.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Hook -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="content-block">
      <p class="lead">
        What if I told you that avoiding a toxic hire is worth <strong>2.3x more</strong> than finding a superstar?
      </p>
      <p>
        That psychological safety creates a <strong>36% revenue swing</strong>? That your "brilliant jerks" are costing you $12,489 each, every year, in people they drive away?
      </p>
      <p>
        These aren't soft HR initiatives. These are hard commercial strategies. And the data is irrefutable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Evidence -->
  <section class="section evidence-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The evidence</h2>
    
    <div class="evidence-grid">
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-number">$12,489</span>
        <span class="evidence-label">The cost of a toxic worker (induced turnover)</span>
        <span class="evidence-compare">vs $5,303 value of a superstar</span>
        <span class="evidence-source">Housman & Minor, Harvard Business School</span>
      </div>
      
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-number">36%</span>
        <span class="evidence-label">Revenue swing from psychological safety</span>
        <span class="evidence-compare">+17% for safe teams, -19% for unsafe</span>
        <span class="evidence-source">Google Project Aristotle</span>
      </div>
      
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-number">$250M</span>
        <span class="evidence-label">Additional annual revenue at Sears</span>
        <span class="evidence-compare">From 5-point employee attitude improvement</span>
        <span class="evidence-source">Sears TPI Model</span>
      </div>
      
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <span class="evidence-number">2.85×</span>
        <span class="evidence-label">More likely Nobel laureates have artistic hobbies</span>
        <span class="evidence-compare">Breadth drives breakthrough</span>
        <span class="evidence-source">Root-Bernstein Research</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Paradox -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The paradox</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p class="lead">
        Toxic workers are often <strong>more productive</strong> than average. That's the trap.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a standard performance dashboard, they look like your best investment. They close deals, ship code, hit targets. But they're a negative-carry asset — their individual gains are offset by the teammates they drive away.
      </p>
      <p>
        The question isn't "Who are our top performers?"
      </p>
      <p class="callout">
        The question is: <strong>"Who's driving our best people to quit?"</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Three Pillars -->
  <section class="section pillars-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The three pillars</h2>
    
    <div class="pillars-grid">
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-number">1</span>
        <h3>Hire for attitude, train for skill</h3>
        <p>Get the right people with the right attitude and they can learn anything. Get the wrong people with the right skills and they'll erode the commercial success you built.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-number">2</span>
        <h3>Listen radically</h3>
        <p>Understand what your people need. Replay it back so you're convinced you understand what must be done. Then do whatever you can — intelligently — to give them the environment to thrive.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-number">3</span>
        <h3>Empower the frontline</h3>
        <p>Give them the tools, the budget, and the permission to solve problems without asking. Ritz-Carlton gives every employee $2,000 per guest. Their turnover dropped from 51% to 23%.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Tool: Manifesto Generator -->
  <section class="section tool-section" id="manifesto-generator">
    <h2 class="section-label">Build your manifesto of permissions</h2>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      The first step to cultural change is making it official. Customise this manifesto, download it, sign it, and put it on the wall. This is how you signal that the rules have changed.
    </p>
    
    <div class="manifesto-builder">
      <div class="manifesto-preview" id="manifestoPreview">
        <div class="manifesto-header">
          <h3>A manifesto of permissions</h3>
          <p class="manifesto-to">To: <span id="audiencePreview">All Colleagues</span></p>
          <p class="manifesto-from">From: <span id="signerPreview">Leadership</span></p>
          <p class="manifesto-date">Date: <span id="datePreview"></span></p>
        </div>
        
        <p class="manifesto-intro">
          For too long, we have operated on a default setting of "wait for permission." This slows us down, stifles your creativity, and erodes our commercial edge.
        </p>
        <p class="manifesto-intro">
          Effective immediately, we are flipping the default. As a member of this team, you officially have:
        </p>
        
        <div class="permissions-list">
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="truth">
            <strong>1. Permission to speak the truth</strong>
            <p>If a process is broken, say it. If a deadline is unrealistic, flag it. If leadership is wrong, challenge it. Silence is not polite; it is dangerous.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="solve">
            <strong>2. Permission to solve the problem</strong>
            <p>If a client is unhappy, fix it. You have the training, the budget, and the judgment. Do not escalate a problem you have the capacity to solve.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="disconnect">
            <strong>3. Permission to disconnect</strong>
            <p>We pay you for your output, not your stamina. You have permission to rest when tired and turn off notifications when deep-working.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="dontknow">
            <strong>4. Permission to say "I don't know"</strong>
            <p>Admitting ignorance is the first step to learning. Blurring the truth to save face is a problem; saying "I don't know, but I will find out" is a badge of honour.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="bypass">
            <strong>5. Permission to bypass bureaucracy</strong>
            <p>If a rule exists solely to tick a box and it prevents you from delivering value, you have permission to question that rule.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="permission active" data-permission="grow">
            <strong>6. Permission to grow (or go)</strong>
            <p>You have permission to outgrow your role. If you feel stagnant, tell us. And if your journey takes you elsewhere, you have permission to leave with our blessing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="manifesto-signature">
          <p>Signed,</p>
          <p class="signature-line" id="signatureLine">_____________________</p>
          <p class="signature-name" id="signatureName">The Leadership Team</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="manifesto-controls">
        <h4>Customise your manifesto</h4>
        
        <label>Who is this for?</label>
        <input type="text" id="audienceInput" value="All Colleagues" placeholder="e.g., The Product Team" />
        
        <label>Who is signing?</label>
        <input type="text" id="signerInput" value="Leadership" placeholder="e.g., The CEO" />
        
        <label>Your name (for signature)</label>
        <input type="text" id="signatureInput" value="The Leadership Team" placeholder="e.g., Jane Smith, CEO" />
        
        <div class="permissions-toggles">
          <label>Include these permissions:</label>
          <div class="toggle-group">
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="truth" checked /> Speak the truth</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="solve" checked /> Solve the problem</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="disconnect" checked /> Disconnect</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="dontknow" checked /> Say "I don't know"</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="bypass" checked /> Bypass bureaucracy</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" data-target="grow" checked /> Grow (or go)</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <button class="download-btn" id="downloadBtn">
          <span>📄</span> Download as PDF
        </button>
        <p class="download-note">Print it. Sign it. Put it on the wall.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tool 2: Safety Thermometer -->
  <section class="section tool-section" id="safety-thermometer">
    <h2 class="section-label">Tool 2: The Safety Thermometer</h2>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      Safety is invisible until it's gone. Use these three questions as a pulse check for your team.
    </p>

    <div class="thermometer-tool">
      <div class="thermometer-questions">
        <div class="t-question">
          <label>1. If you made a mistake on this project, would it be held against you?</label>
          <div class="t-options">
            <button class="t-btn danger" onclick="updateThermometer(1, 0)">Yes</button>
            <button class="t-btn safe" onclick="updateThermometer(1, 10)">No</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="t-question">
          <label>2. Is it easy to ask other members of this team for help?</label>
          <div class="t-options">
            <button class="t-btn safe" onclick="updateThermometer(2, 10)">Yes</button>
            <button class="t-btn danger" onclick="updateThermometer(2, 0)">No</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="t-question">
          <label>3. Have you seen anyone on this team deliberately undermine others?</label>
          <div class="t-options">
            <button class="t-btn danger" onclick="updateThermometer(3, 0)">Yes</button>
            <button class="t-btn safe" onclick="updateThermometer(3, 10)">No</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="thermometer-result" id="thermometerResult">
        <div class="t-meter">
          <div class="t-level" id="tLevel"></div>
        </div>
        <h4 id="tStatus">Check your temperature</h4>
        <p id="tDesc">Select answers to see your safety score.</p>
        <div class="t-revenue" id="tRevenue">
          <span>Projected Revenue Impact:</span>
          <strong id="tImpact">--</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tool 3: Smoke Detector -->
  <section class="section tool-section" id="smoke-detector">
    <h2 class="section-label">Tool 3: The Smoke Detector</h2>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      Identify the "brilliant jerks" before they burn down your culture. Answer these for a specific high-performer.
    </p>

    <div class="smoke-detector-tool">
      <div class="smoke-grid">
        <div class="smoke-q">
          <label>The Credit Test</label>
          <p>Do they say "I" or "We" when things go well?</p>
          <select id="smoke1" onchange="checkSmoke()">
            <option value="0">Select...</option>
            <option value="safe">Mostly "We"</option>
            <option value="risk">Mostly "I"</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="smoke-q">
          <label>The Error Response</label>
          <p>When others make a mistake, do they help or blame?</p>
          <select id="smoke2" onchange="checkSmoke()">
            <option value="0">Select...</option>
            <option value="safe">Help/Teach</option>
            <option value="risk">Blame/Mock</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="smoke-q">
          <label>The Energy Exchange</label>
          <p>Do you feel drained or energised after meeting them?</p>
          <select id="smoke3" onchange="checkSmoke()">
            <option value="0">Select...</option>
            <option value="safe">Energised</option>
            <option value="risk">Drained</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="smoke-q">
          <label>The Unseen Work</label>
          <p>Do they do work that doesn't get them credit?</p>
          <select id="smoke4" onchange="checkSmoke()">
            <option value="0">Select...</option>
            <option value="safe">Yes, often</option>
            <option value="risk">Never</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="smoke-q">
          <label>The Lifeboat Question</label>
          <p>If you were starting a new company, would you hire them?</p>
          <select id="smoke5" onchange="checkSmoke()">
            <option value="0">Select...</option>
            <option value="safe">Absolutely</option>
            <option value="risk">No way</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="smoke-result" id="smokeResult" style="display:none;">
        <h3 id="smokeTitle">Status...</h3>
        <p id="smokeDesc">Diagnosis...</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Pilot -->
  <section class="section pilot-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The 90-day pilot</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p class="lead">
        We don't ask you to transform the whole business. We ask you to run an experiment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Take one team. Apply The Greenhouse. Document the results. Let them prove what's possible.
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="pilot-planner-tool">
      <div class="pp-header">
        <label>Pilot Start Date:</label>
        <input type="date" id="pilotStartDate" onchange="updatePilot()" />
      </div>

      <div class="pilot-phases interactive" id="pilotPhases">
        <!-- Rendered by JS -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tool 5: New World Dictionary -->
  <section class="section tool-section" id="dictionary">
    <h2 class="section-label">Tool 5: The New World Dictionary</h2>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      Language shapes reality. Stop using factory terms for creative work.
    </p>
    <div class="dictionary-grid">
      <div class="dict-card">
        <span class="old-word">Human Resources</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="new-word">People & Potential</span>
        <p>We cultivate talent, we don't extract it like coal.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dict-card">
        <span class="old-word">Manager</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="new-word">Blocker Remover</span>
        <p>Your job is to remove obstacles, not issue commands.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dict-card">
        <span class="old-word">Soft Skills</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="new-word">Power Skills</span>
        <p>The only skills AI cannot replicate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dict-card">
        <span class="old-word">Performance Review</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="new-word">Alignment Session</span>
        <p>Don't judge the past. Align the future.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dict-card">
        <span class="old-word">Failure</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="new-word">Tuition</span>
        <p>The price we pay for learning something new.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Ready to run The Greenhouse?</h2>
    <p>Let's find your most expensive person — and turn them into your best investment.</p>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com?subject=The%20Greenhouse%20Pilot" class="cta-button">Start the Conversation →</a>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .greenhouse-hero {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-label {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.15);
    color: #4CAF50;
    padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .greenhouse-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .content-block {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.4rem !important;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .callout {
    font-size: 1.5rem !important;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05);
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  /* Evidence Grid */
  .evidence-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .evidence-card {
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #222;
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .evidence-number {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .evidence-label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .evidence-compare {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .evidence-source {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: #555;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  /* Pillars */
  .pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .pillar {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 3.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-number {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .pillar h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pillar p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Manifesto Tool */
  .tool-section {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 4rem 0;
  }

  .tool-section .section-label,
  .tool-section .tool-intro {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .tool-intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .manifesto-builder {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 320px;
    gap: 3rem;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .manifesto-preview {
    background: #fff;
    color: #111;
    padding: 3rem;
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .manifesto-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #111;
  }

  .manifesto-header h3 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .manifesto-header p {
    margin: 0.3rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .manifesto-intro {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .permissions-list {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .permission {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid #111;
    transition: opacity 0.3s;
  }

  .permission:not(.active) {
    opacity: 0.2;
  }

  .permission strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
  }

  .permission p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .manifesto-signature {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
  }

  .signature-line {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .signature-name {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Controls */
  .manifesto-controls {
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #222;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .manifesto-controls h4 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .manifesto-controls label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .manifesto-controls input[type="text"] {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    background: #0a0a0a;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .manifesto-controls input[type="text"]:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .permissions-toggles {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .toggle-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .toggle-group label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toggle-group input[type="checkbox"] {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .download-btn {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #000;
    border: none;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .download-btn:hover {
    background: #ff8a50;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .download-note {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  /* Pilot Phases */
  .pilot-phases {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .phase {
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #222;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .phase-label {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .phase h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .phase p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 6rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #000;
    padding: 1rem 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  }

  .dict-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .old-word {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: line-through;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .arrow {
    display: block;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .new-word {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .dict-card p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #ccc;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .manifesto-builder {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .manifesto-controls {
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Set today's date
  document.getElementById('datePreview').textContent = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
    day: 'numeric',
    month: 'long',
    year: 'numeric'
  });

  // Live preview updates
  document.getElementById('audienceInput').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    document.getElementById('audiencePreview').textContent = e.target.value || 'All Colleagues';
  });

  document.getElementById('signerInput').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    document.getElementById('signerPreview').textContent = e.target.value || 'Leadership';
  });

  document.getElementById('signatureInput').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    document.getElementById('signatureName').textContent = e.target.value || 'The Leadership Team';
  });

  // Permission toggles
  document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-group input[type="checkbox"]').forEach(checkbox => {
    checkbox.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const target = e.target.dataset.target;
      const permission = document.querySelector(`.permission[data-permission="${target}"]`);
      if (permission) {
        permission.classList.toggle('active', e.target.checked);
      }
    });
  });

  // Download functionality
  document.getElementById('downloadBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const manifestoHTML = document.getElementById('manifestoPreview').innerHTML;
    const audience = document.getElementById('audienceInput').value || 'All Colleagues';
    const signer = document.getElementById('signerInput').value || 'Leadership';
    const signatureName = document.getElementById('signatureInput').value || 'The Leadership Team';
    
    // Create printable version
    const printWindow = window.open('', '_blank');
    printWindow.document.write(`
      <!DOCTYPE html>
      <html>
      <head>
        <title>Manifesto of Permissions</title>
        <style>
          body {
            font-family: Georgia, serif;
            max-width: 700px;
            margin: 2rem auto;
            padding: 2rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
          }
          h3 {
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
            padding-bottom: 1rem;
          }
          .permission {
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            padding-left: 1rem;
            border-left: 3px solid #000;
          }
          .permission:not(.active) {
            display: none;
          }
          .signature-line {
            margin-top: 3rem;
            border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding-top: 2rem;
          }
          @media print {
            body { margin: 0; padding: 1.5rem; }
          }
        </style>
      </head>
      <body>
        ${manifestoHTML}
      </body>
      </html>
    `);
    printWindow.document.close();
    printWindow.print();
  });

  /* --- TOOLS JS --- */
  
  // Safety Thermometer Logic
  let tScores = {1: null, 2: null, 3: null};
  
  window.updateThermometer = (q, score) => {
    tScores[q] = score;
    
    // UI Update
    const questionDiv = document.querySelectorAll('.t-question')[q-1];
    const btns = questionDiv.querySelectorAll('.t-btn');
    btns.forEach(b => b.classList.remove('selected'));
    
    // Find clicked button based on onclick attribute... simplified:
    // Just re-selecting based on class isnt enough.
    // Let's rely on the button passed in scope? No, easier to just check class match in loop if possible, 
    // or just assume the click handler works. 
    // Actually, to style the selected button, I need a reference.
    // Let's use event delegation or just simple loop in the click.
    // For simplicity here, I'll cheat and use `event.target`.
  };

  // Re-define global function to use event
  window.updateThermometer = function(q, score) {
    tScores[q] = score;
    const btn = event.target;
    const parent = btn.parentElement;
    parent.querySelectorAll('.t-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('selected'));
    btn.classList.add('selected');

    // Calc result
    if (Object.values(tScores).every(v => v !== null)) {
      const total = Object.values(tScores).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
      const level = document.getElementById('tLevel');
      const status = document.getElementById('tStatus');
      const desc = document.getElementById('tDesc');
      const impact = document.getElementById('tImpact');
      
      const pct = (total / 30) * 100;
      level.style.width = pct + '%';
      
      if (total < 15) {
        status.textContent = "Critical Condition";
        status.style.color = "#d32f2f";
        desc.textContent = "Psychological safety is absent. Honest errors are hidden, preventing learning.";
        impact.textContent = "-19% Revenue Impact";
      } else if (total < 25) {
        status.textContent = "Stable but Stagnant";
        status.style.color = "#fbc02d";
        desc.textContent = "People are polite but guarded. Innovation is stifled by caution.";
        impact.textContent = "Neutral Impact";
      } else {
        status.textContent = "High Performance Zone";
        status.style.color = "#388e3c";
        desc.textContent = "Your team feels safe to take risks. Errors are treated as tuition.";
        impact.textContent = "+17% Revenue Impact";
      }
    }
  };

  // Smoke Detector Logic
  window.checkSmoke = function() {
    const selects = [1,2,3,4,5].map(i => document.getElementById('smoke'+i));
    if (selects.some(s => s.value === "0")) return; // Wait for all

    const riskCount = selects.filter(s => s.value === 'risk').length;
    const result = document.getElementById('smokeResult');
    const title = document.getElementById('smokeTitle');
    const desc = document.getElementById('smokeDesc');
    
    result.style.display = 'block';
    
    if (riskCount >= 3) {
      result.style.border = "2px solid #d32f2f";
      result.style.background = "rgba(211, 47, 47, 0.1)";
      title.textContent = "High Risk: Cultural Arsonist";
      title.style.color = "#d32f2f";
      desc.innerHTML = "This person is likely a negative-carry asset. Their individual output is being cancelled out by the friction they create.<br><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Immediate feedback. If behavior doesn't change in 30 days, exit.";
    } else {
      result.style.border = "2px solid #388e3c";
      result.style.background = "rgba(56, 142, 60, 0.1)";
      title.textContent = "Low Risk: True High Performer";
      title.style.color = "#388e3c";
      desc.textContent = "This person adds value to the culture as well as the P&L. Clone them.";
    }
  };

  // Pilot Planner Logic
  window.updatePilot = function() {
    const startInput = document.getElementById('pilotStartDate').value;
    if (!startInput) return;
    
    const start = new Date(startInput);
    const container = document.getElementById('pilotPhases');
    
    const formatDate = (d) => d.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {day: 'numeric', month: 'short'});
    const addDays = (d, days) => {
      const result = new Date(d);
      result.setDate(result.getDate() + days);
      return result;
    };

    const dates = {
      baseStart: addDays(start, -7),
      resetStart: start,
      empowerStart: addDays(start, 30),
      accelStart: addDays(start, 60),
      end: addDays(start, 90)
    };

    container.innerHTML = `
      <div class="phase">
        <span class="phase-label">Week -1 (${formatDate(dates.baseStart)})</span>
        <h4>Baseline</h4>
        <p>Time audit, pulse survey, commercial metrics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <span class="phase-label">Days 1-30 (${formatDate(dates.resetStart)})</span>
        <h4>The Reset</h4>
        <p>Manifesto kick-off, "Stupid Rule Bonfire".</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <span class="phase-label">Days 31-60 (${formatDate(dates.empowerStart)})</span>
        <h4>The Empowerment</h4>
        <p>Agency budgets given. "Blocks & Blockers" check-ins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <span class="phase-label">Days 61-90 (${formatDate(dates.accelStart)})</span>
        <h4>The Acceleration</h4>
        <p>Alignment sessions. Final results comparison: ${formatDate(dates.end)}.</p>
      </div>
    `;
  };

  // set default pilot date
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    document.getElementById('pilotStartDate').valueAsDate = new Date();
    updatePilot();
  });
</script>
</Base>
